From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 03:21:03 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/35] clk: samsung: exynos9610: register the CMU_TOP
 FSYS_UFS_EMBD divider

The FSYS clock 'mout_pll_fsys_ufs_embd_user' names 'dout_cmu_fsys_ufs_embd'
as its parent and the binding passes CLK_DOUT_CMU_FSYS_UFS_EMBD to CMU_FSYS,
but CMU_TOP never registered that divider, so the UFS UniPro clock was an
orphan at 0 Hz on the Galaxy A50. Field per Samsung's CAL
(CLK_CON_DIV_CLKCMU_FSYS_UFS_EMBD_DIVRATIO, bit 0, width 4).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I8841c9cf77da29029a0fbaf74937b1f4a411710f
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9610.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9610.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9610.c
index 7e7284541..fef245c14 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9610.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9610.c
@@ -665,6 +665,8 @@ static const struct samsung_div_clock top_div_clks[] __initconst = {
 	    CLK_CON_DIV_CLKCMU_FSYS_MMC_CARD, 0, 9),
 	DIV(CLK_DOUT_CMU_FSYS_MMC_EMBD, "dout_cmu_fsys_mmc_embd", "gout_cmu_fsys_mmc_embd",
 	    CLK_CON_DIV_CLKCMU_FSYS_MMC_EMBD, 0, 9),
+	DIV(CLK_DOUT_CMU_FSYS_UFS_EMBD, "dout_cmu_fsys_ufs_embd", "gout_cmu_fsys_ufs_embd",
+	    CLK_CON_DIV_CLKCMU_FSYS_UFS_EMBD, 0, 4),
 	DIV(CLK_DOUT_CMU_G2D_G2D, "dout_cmu_g2d_g2d", "gout_cmu_g2d_g2d",
 	    CLK_CON_DIV_CLKCMU_G2D_G2D, 0, 4),
 	DIV(CLK_DOUT_CMU_G2D_MSCL, "dout_cmu_g2d_mscl", "gout_cmu_g2d_mscl",
